(6414475, 950763, 42495, '<td valign="top">The first thing that grabs me is that what appears to be your main subject, the tape or whatever it is, looks more brownish than gold, at least on my monitor.  Some of the creases it in look quite golden to me and I would have preferred the whole thing to have that hue.  If I were voting I would not deduct for the color, it''s close enough.<br/> <br/>Your idea here is fascinating and while it doesn''t have mainstream DPC appeal it does have an audience.  This photo really works for me because the person behind is blurred and the tape just adds another layer of obfuscation.  The hand is a nice touch and contrasts nicely with the background.<br/> <br/>IMO, it would be a stronger image if it were cropped differently, maybe a bit off the right or even in portrait orientation.  Having a smaller strip over just the mouth may give it a different feel.</td>', 'The first thing that grabs me is that what appears to be your main subject, the tape or whatever it is, looks more brownish than gold, at least on my monitor.  Some of the creases it in look quite golden to me and I would have preferred the whole thing to have that hue.  If I were voting I would not deduct for the color, it''s close enough. Your idea here is fascinating and while it doesn''t have mainstream DPC appeal it does have an audience.  This photo really works for me because the person behind is blurred and the tape just adds another layer of obfuscation.  The hand is a nice touch and contrasts nicely with the background. IMO, it would be a stronger image if it were cropped differently, maybe a bit off the right or even in portrait orientation.  Having a smaller strip over just the mouth may give it a different feel.', '2011-05-15 23:54:05.000000', NULL, 1),
